Extra supplementary groups for the runtime user.

Drop a `<feature>.conf` here listing one group name per line (`#`
starts a comment). On every boot mybox-user-setup.service unions these
with its base set (wheel video render input audio kvm libvirt) and
`gpasswd -a`s the runtime user into each group that EXISTS at that
moment; groups whose package is not installed are skipped silently and
retried next boot.

Why a drop-in dir instead of editing user-setup: a layered variant
image (`FROM ghcr.io/aboglioli/mybox:<tag>`) that installs docker,
wireshark or plugdev-owning packages ships its own file here and needs
no patch to the base script. Same reason the packages themselves land
in the /usr overlay rather than the image.

Slot convention matches /usr/share/mybox/just/: 00-49 shipped, 50-99
local additions.

Example — /usr/share/mybox/user-groups.d/50-docker.conf:

    # rootful docker socket access inside the container
    docker

Binding is add-only: removing a file here does not strip the
membership from /etc/group. Prune it by hand (`gpasswd -d <user>
<group>`) if that matters.
